INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Incline Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Place an incline banc underneath the smith machine. Place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Once the poids you need is selected, Allongez-vous sur un banc incliné and make sure your upper poitrine is aligned with the barre. Using a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant) that is wider than épaule width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your upper poitrine.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Incline_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Leg Press', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. Position a Smith machine bar a couple feet off of the ground. Ensure that it is resting on the safeties. After loading the bar to an appropriate poids, lie underneath the bar. Place the middle of vos pieds on the bar, tucking your genous to your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement by driving through vos pieds to move the bar upward, extending the hanches and genous. Do not lock out your genous.
3. At the top of the motion, pause briefly before returning to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Leg_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine One-Arm Upright Row', 'Épaules', 'Machine', '1. With the bar at cuisse level, load an appropriate poids.
2. Take a prise large on the bar and unhook the poids, removing your off hand from the bar. Your arm should be extended as you Tenez-vous debout avec votre tête and poitrine up. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin le mouvement by flexing the coude, raising the upper arm with the coude pointed out. Continue until your upper arm is parallèle au sol.
4. Après une pause, return the poids to the position de départ.
5. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions before engaging the hooks to rack the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_One-Arm_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Overhead Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Machine', '1. To begin, place a flat banc (or preferably one with back support) underneath a smith machine. Position the barre at a height so that when seated on the flat banc, the arms must be almost fully extended to reach the barre.
2. Once you have the correct height, sit slightly in behind the barre so that there is an imaginary straight line from the tip of your nose to the barre. vos pieds should be stationary. Grab the barre with the paumes vers l''avant, unlock it and lift it up so that vos bras are fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, begin to lower the barre until it is level with your chin while inhaling.
4. Then lift the barre back to the position de départ using your épaules while exhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Overhead_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Pistol Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, first set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Step under it and position the bar across the back of your épaules.
2. Take the bar with vos mains facing forward, unlock it and lift it off the rack by extending vos jambes. 3
3. Move one foot forward about 12 inches in front of the bar. Extend the other leg out in front of you, holding it off the ground. Look forward en permanence and maintain a neutral or slightly arched spine. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Maintaining good posture, lower yourself by flexing the genou and hanche, going down as far as flexibility allows.
5. Pause briefly at the bottom and then Revenez en position de départ by driving through the heel of your foot, extending the genou and hanche.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Pistol_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Reverse Calf Raises', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the barre on the smith machine to fit your height and align a raised platform right under the bar.
2. Stand on the platform with the heels of vos pieds secured on top of it with the balls of vos pieds extending off it. Position your toes facing forward with a épaule width stance.
3. Now, place your épaules under the barre while maintaining the foot positioning described and push the barre up by extending your hanches and genous until your torse is standing erect. The genous should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : The barre on votre dos is only for balance purposes.
4. Raise the balls of vos pieds as you Expirez by extending your toes as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Maintenez la position 1 seconde before you start to go back down.
5. Lentement, go back down to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering the balls of vos pieds and toes.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Reverse_Calf_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, first set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (paumes vers l''avant), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Stiff-Legged Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your cuisses. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is épaule width apart. You may need some poignet wraps if using a significant amount of poids.
2. Lift the bar up by fully extending vos bras while keeping votre dos straight. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a épaule width or narrower stance. The genous should be slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the genous stationary, lower the barre to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the waist while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Expirez as you perform this movement
4. Start bringing your torse up straight again as soon as you feel the ischio-jambiers stretch by extending your hanches and waist until you are back at the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Stiff-Legged_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Upright Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Machine', '1. To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your cuisses. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is épaule width apart. You may need some poignet wraps if using a significant amount of poids.
2. Lift the barre up and fully extend vos bras with votre dos straight. There should be a slight bend at the coudes. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Use your side épaules to lift the bar as you expirez. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the bar, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
4. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Single-Leg Split Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, place a flat banc 2-3 feet behind the smith machine. Then, set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (paumes vers l''avant), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Position vos jambes by placing one foot slightly forward under the bar and extending your other leg back and place the top of your foot on the banc. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genou as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calf becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genou should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genou is past that imaginary line (if it is past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten your leg again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. Switch legs and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Single-Leg_Split_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Place vos pieds at a épaule width stance with the barre resting right above the connection between the toes and the rest of the foot.
2. With a paumes vers down grip, bend at the genous and keeping the back flat grab the bar using a wider than épaule width grip. Bring the hanches down and make sure that votre corps drops as if you were going to sit on a chair. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Start pushing le sol as if it were a moving platform with vos pieds and simultaneously start lifting the barre keeping it close to vos jambes.
4. As the bar reaches the middle of your cuisses, push le sol with vos jambes and lift votre corps to a complete extension in an explosive motion.
5. Lift your épaules back in a shrugging movement as you bring the bar up while lifting your coudes out to the side and keeping them above the bar for as long as possible.
6. Now in a very quick but powerful motion, you have to get votre corps under the barre when it has reached a high enough point where it can be controlled and drop while locking vos bras and holding the barre overhead as you assume a squat position.
7. Finalize le mouvement by rising up out of the squat position to finish the lift. At the end of the lift both feet should be on line and the arms fully extended holding the barre overhead.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Balance', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with the feet in the pulling position, the bar racked across the back of the épaules, and the hands placed in a wide snatch grip.
2. Pop the bar with an abrupt dip and drive of the genous, and aggressively drive under the bar, transitioning the feet into the receiving position.
3. Receive the bar locked out overhead near the bottom of the squat. The torse should remain vertical, lowering the hanches between the legs.
4. Continue to descend to full depth, and return to a standing position. Carefully lower the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Balance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. The snatch deadlift strengthens the first pull of the snatch. Begin with a wide snatch grip with the barre placed on the platform. The feet should be directly under the hanches, with the feet turned out. Squat down to the bar, keeping the back in absolute extension with the head facing forward.
2. Initiate le mouvement by driving through the heels, raising the hanches. The back angle should remain the same until the bar passes the genous.
3. At that point, drive your hanches through the bar as you lay back. Return the bar to the platform by reversing the motion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Pull', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take a wide snatch grip. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genous.
3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the pull. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward.
4. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back. Full extension should be violent and abrupt, and ensure that you do not prolong the extension for longer than necessary.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a prise large, with the bar hanging at the mid cuisse position. You can use a hook or prise en pronation. votre dos should be straight and inclined slightly forward.
2. Shrug your épaules towards your ears. While cet exercice can usually by loaded with heavier poids than a snatch, avoid overloading to the point that the execution slows down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch from Blocks', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on boxes or stands of the desired height. A prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hanches, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hanches, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The épaules should be just in front of the bar, with the coudes pointed out. This will be the position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the boxes.
3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hanches genous and chevilles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move to just outside the hanches, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.
5. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, votre tête and poitrine up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the poids to the boxes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_from_Blocks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Band Overhead Triceps', 'Triceps', 'Élastique', '1. For cet exercice anchor a band to the ground. We used an incline banc and anchored the band to the base, standing over the banc. Alternatively, this could be performed standing on the band.
2. To begin, pull the band behind votre tête, holding it with a pronated grip and your coudes up. C''est votre position de départ.
3. To perform le mouvement, extend through the coude to to straighten vos bras, ensuring that you keep your upper arm in place.
4. Pause, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Band_Overhead_Triceps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Box Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Attach bands to the bar that are securely anchored near the ground. You may need to choke the bands to get adequate tension.
2. Use a box of an appropriate height for cet exercice. Load the bar to a poids that still requires effort, but isn''t so heavy that speed is compromised. Typically, that will be between 50-70% of your one rep max.
3. Position the bar on your upper back, omoplates retracted, back arched and everything tight head to toe. This will be the position de départ.
4. Unrack the bar and position yourself in front of the box. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box, ensuring that you descend under control and don''t crash onto the surface.
5. Pause briefly, and explode off of the box, extending through the hanches and genous.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Box_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
4. Begin to lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as fast as possible without involving momentum as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ. Note: You should perform these exercises as fast as possible but without breaking perfect form and without involving momentum.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spell Caster', 'Abdominaux', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a haltère in each hand with a pronated grip. vos pieds should be wide with your hanches and genous extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement by pulling both of the haltères to one side next to your hanche, rotating your torse.
3. Keeping vos bras straight and the haltères parallel to the ground, rotate your torse to swing the poids to your opposite side.
4. Continue alternating, rotating from one side to the other until the set is complete.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spell_Caster/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spider Crawl', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a prone position on le sol. Support your poids on vos mains and toes, with vos pieds together and votre corps straight. vos bras should be bent to 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement by raising one foot off of the ground. Externally rotate the leg and bring the genou toward your coude, as far forward as possible.
3. Return this leg to the position de départ and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spider_Crawl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spider Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Start out by setting the bar on the part of the preacher banc that you would normally sit on. Make sure to align the barre properly so that it is balanced and will not fall off.
2. Move to the front side of the preacher banc (the part where the arms usually lay) and position yourself to lay at a 45 degree slant with your torse and stomach pressed against the front side of the preacher banc.
3. Make sure that vos pieds (especially the toes) are well positioned on le sol and place your upper arms on top of the pad located on the inside part of the preacher banc.
4. Use vos bras to grab the barre with a supinated grip (paumes vers up) at about épaule width apart or slightly closer from each other.
5. Lentement, begin to lift the barre upwards and expirez. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
6. Lentement, begin to bring the barre back to the position de départ as your Inspirez. .
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spider_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spinal Stretch', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Sit in a chair so votre dos is straight and vos pieds planted on le sol.
2. Interlace your fingers behind votre tête, coudes out and your chin down.
3. Twist your upper body to one side about 3 times as far as you can. Then lean forward and twist your torse to reach your coude to le sol on the inside of your genou.
4. Return to upright position and then Répétez for your other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Bas du dos, Cou, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spinal_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Clean', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take an prise en pronation just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genous.
3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.
4. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so.
5. Receive the bar with the feet split, aggressively moving one foot forward and one foot back. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom position, which will help in the recovery.
6. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Bring the feet together as you Levez-vous.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Jerk', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the épaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hanches, flex the genous without moving the hanches backward.
2. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move votre tête out of the way as the bar leaves the épaules. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible.
3. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athlete''s effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should be moved to a split stance, one foot forward, one foot back, with the genous partially bent. Receive the bar with the arms locked out overhead.
4. Return to a standing position, bringing the feet together.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a lunge stance position with one foot forward with the genou bent, and the rear genou nearly touching the ground.
2. Ensure that the front genou is over the midline of the foot.
3. Extending through both legs, jump as high as possible, swinging vos bras to gain lift.
4. As you jump, bring vos pieds together, and move them back to their initial positions as you land.
5. Absorb the impact by reverting back to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Snatch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on le sol. The bar should be close to or touching the shins, and a prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hanches, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hanches, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The épaules should be just in front of the bar. This will be the position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the ground. The back angle should stay the same until the bar passes the genous.
3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hanches genous and chevilles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move forcefully to a split position, one foot forward one foot back. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.
5. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, votre tête and poitrine up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position, bringing vos pieds together.
6. Carefully return the poids to floor.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Squat with Dumbbells', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Position yourself into a staggered stance with the rear foot elevated and front foot forward.
2. Hold a haltère in each hand, letting them hang at the sides. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by descending, flexing your genou and hanche to lower votre corps down. Maintain good posture througout le mouvement. Keep the front genou in line with the foot as you perform the exercise.
4. At the bottom of le mouvement, drive through the heel to extend the genou and hanche to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Squat_with_Dumbbells/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Squats', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Being in a standing position. Jump into a split leg position, with one leg forward and one leg back, flexing the genous and lowering your hanches slightly as you do so.
2. As you descend, immediately reverse direction, standing back up and jumping, reversing the position of vos jambes. Répétez 5-10 times on each leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat Jerk', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the épaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hanches, flex the genous without moving the hanches backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move votre tête out of the way as the bar leaves the épaules.
2. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athlete''s effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should move forcefully to just outside the hanches, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with votre corps in a full squat and the arms fully extended overhead.
3. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, votre tête and poitrine up, drive throught heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the poids to floor.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Bands', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Set up the bands on the sleeves, secured to either band pegs, the rack, or haltères so that there is appropriate tension.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wide for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers. Keep votre tête facing forward.
3. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torse lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hanche being in line with the top of the genou.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Chains', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. To set up the chains, begin by looping the leader chain over the sleeves of the bar. The heavy chain should be attached using a snap hook. Adjust the length of the lead chain so that a few links are still on le sol at the top of le mouvement.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wide for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers. Keep votre tête facing forward.
3. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torse lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hanche being in line with the top of the genou.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Plate Movers', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. To begin, first set the bar on a rack to just below épaule level. Position a poids plate on the ground a couple feet back from the rack. Once the bar is loaded, step under it and place the back of your épaules across it.
2. Hold on to the bar with both hands and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straighten your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and adopt a wide stance with the toes slightly pointed out, with one foot on the poids plate. Keep votre tête up en permanence. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous and hanches. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees.
5. Raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heels of vos pieds as you extend the hanches and genous.
6. At the top of le mouvement, side step, bringing vos pieds together on the opposite side of the plate.
7. Using your inside foot, push the poids plate, sliding it across le sol to where you were just standing.
8. Place your inside foot on the poids plate, adopting a wide stance for the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Plate_Movers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squats - With Bands', 'Quadriceps', 'Élastique', '1. To start out, make sure that the exercise band is at an even split between both the left and right side of the body. To do this, use vos mains to grab both sides of the band and place both feet in the middle of the band. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other.
2. When holding the bands, they should be the same height on each side. You should be using a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant) and have the handles of the bands next to your face for cet exercice. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, start to bend the genous and lower the legs so that your cuisses are parallèle au sol while exhaling.
4. Use the heel of vos pieds to push votre corps up to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squats_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stairmaster', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the stairmaster and select the desired option from the menu. You can choose a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise.
2. Pump vos jambes up and down in an established rhythm, driving the pedals down but not all the way to le sol. It is recommended that you maintain your grip on the handles so that you don''t fall. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity.
3. Stairmasters offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside. They are typically much harder than other cardio equipment. A 150 lb person will typically burn over 300 calories in 30 minutes, compared to about 175 calories walking.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stairmaster/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Alternating Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère in each hand. Raise the haltères to your épaules with your paumes vers l''avant and your coudes pointed out. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Extend one arm to press the haltère straight up, keeping your off hand in place. Do not lean or jerk the poids during le mouvement.
3. Après une pause, return the poids to the position de départ.
4. Répétez de l''autre côté, continuing to alternate between arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Alternating_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Barbell Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the bar on the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck).
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. The genous should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : For better range of motion you may also place the ball of vos pieds on a wooden block but be careful as this option requires more balance and a sturdy block.
4. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your chevilles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
5. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the chevilles until mollets are stretched.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Barbell_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Barbell Press Behind Neck', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for easier pick up of the bar. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. votre dos should be kept straight while performing cet exercice. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Elevate the barre overhead by fully extending vos bras while breathing out.
5. Hold the contraction for a second and lower the barre back down to the position de départ by inhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Barbell_Press_Behind_Neck/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. With a haltère in one hand and the paumes vers your torse, bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Make sure that you keep the head up.
2. The upper arm should be close to the torse and parallèle au sol while the forearm is pointing towards le sol as the hand holds the poids. Conseil : There should be a angle de 90 degrés between the forearm and the upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids as you expirez until the forearms are parallèle au sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.
4. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltère back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
6. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. With a haltère in each hand and the paumes vers your torse, bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Make sure that you keep the head up. The upper arms should be close to the torse and parallèle au sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids. Conseil : There should be a angle de 90 degrés between the forearms and the upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids as you expirez until the forearms are parallèle au sol and the whole arms are extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.
3. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltères back to their position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Biceps Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a cable curl bar that is attached to a low pulley. Grab the cable bar at épaule width and keep the coudes close to the torse. The palm of vos mains should be facing up (supinated grip). C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the curl bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Biceps_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Biceps Stretch', 'Biceps', 'Autre', '1. Clasp vos mains behind votre dos with your palms together, straighten arms and then rotate them so your palms face downward.
2. Raise vos bras up and hold until you feel a stretch in your biceps.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Biceps_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bradford Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Place a loaded bar at épaule level in a rack. With a pronated grip at épaule width, begin with the bar racked across the front of your épaules. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate the lift by extending the coudes to press the bar overhead. Avoid locking out the coude as you move the poids behind votre tête.
3. Lower the bar down to the back of the head until your coude forms a right angle.
4. Lift the bar back over votre tête by extending the coudes
